data.content:
Your project targets **net10.0** and your `ReportGenerator` uses `File.WriteAllText`, `Directory.Exists`, `Directory.CreateDirectory`, plus other statics. The best approach for file system statics is the **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — it's battle-tested and provides a complete `IFileSystem` abstraction.

## Recommended approach: `System.IO.Abstractions`

**1. Install the package:**
```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

**2. Inject `IFileSystem` into your class:**
```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_...");
        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

**3. Register in DI (Program.cs):**
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

**4. Test with `MockFileSystem`:**
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```
```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("Sales");

Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
var content = mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path);
Assert.Contains("Sales", content);
```

## Bonus: your file also has other statics

Your `ReportGenerator` has **5 categories** of statics beyond filesystem:

| Static | Recommended abstraction |
|---|---|
| `DateTime.UtcNow` | **`TimeProvider`** (built-in on .NET 10) — inject `TimeProvider`, use `timeProvider.GetUtcNow()` |
| `Environment.*` | Custom **`IEnvironmentProvider`** wrapper (only wrap `GetEnvironmentVariable` + `MachineName`) |
| `Console.WriteLine` | Custom **`IConsole`** wrapper or use `ILogger<T>` instead |

`TimeProvider` is the easiest win — just register `builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System)` and inject it. In tests, use `FakeTimeProvider` from `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`.

